INT. SAFE HOUSE, TOP FLOOR OF A CLOSED HOTEL - NIGHT

Plaster dust. A bare bed frame. Window shutters nailed shut. On the floor, a battered radio set squats between two chairs.

DETECTIVE MIRELA VASQUEZ-ODEH (40s, trench coat, a revolver at her hip) sits in one chair, back to the wall. Opposite her, a man in a gray suit, STRANGER (50s, ink-stained fingers, a gauze patch on his neck), sits with his hands in his lap.

VASQUEZ-ODEH
You've been very quiet.

STRANGER
You haven't asked me anything.

VASQUEZ-ODEH
I'm asking now. Who are you?

STRANGER
A man who works for the people who want me dead.

VASQUEZ-ODEH
That's not a name.

STRANGER
It's the only name I carry safely.

The radio crackles. A clipped voice breaks through, distorted. It is his voice. The man in the chair has not moved his lips.

STRANGER (V.O.)
(recorded, his own voice, flattened by the speaker)
Unit Four, this is Control. Confirm subject in custody.

Vasquez-Odeh picks up the handset, eyes on him.

VASQUEZ-ODEH
Control, subject is in custody. Repeat, subject is secure.

STRANGER (V.O.)
Copy. Transport in twenty. Stand by.

She sets the handset down. He watches her do it.

STRANGER
They aren't coming for me. They're coming for you.

VASQUEZ-ODEH
You'd say that.

STRANGER
I'd say it because it's true. Control is a tape. I recorded it myself, in March. You've been talking to an empty room for an hour.

She draws the revolver. Aims. He doesn't flinch.

VASQUEZ-ODEH
What's your name?

STRANGER
Anselm Ravindran.

She lowers the revolver an inch.

VASQUEZ-ODEH
That's the name on the file. The one who was supposed to be dead.

ANSELM
I was. Then I wasn't. Look at the window.

She keeps the gun level, but her eyes slide to the shutters. A thin line of light moves behind the slats: a flashlight, sweeping.

VASQUEZ-ODEH
(whispering)
Transport already?

ANSELM
That's not transport.

The door handle turns. They both rise, each knocking over a chair. He lunges for the radio. She lunges for the door. Their shoulders collide. The radio tumbles; the handset swings on its cord.

STRANGER (V.O.)
...Unit Four, report. Unit Four...

Anselm kills the power. Silence. The doorknob stops turning. Then, from the hall, a soft, regretful click, as of a pistol being cocked.

VASQUEZ-ODEH
(barely audible)
Window.

ANSELM
Nailed shut.

VASQUEZ-ODEH
Then the ceiling.

She points to a rotted panel. He nods. They climb.
